  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to the definition of \"veteran\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S5819",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5819-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 44,
       "fullName": "Neil D. Breslin",
       "imgName": "372_neil_d._breslin.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 372,
       "sessionMemberId": 1201,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "BRESLIN"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §357, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5819\n\nSPONSOR: METZGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to the\ndefinition of \"veteran\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide those veteran who have served during peacetime to be eligible\nfor the position of a county veterans' service agency director.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Subdivisions 1 and 2 of Section 357 of the Executive Law,\nSubdivision 1 is amended to include within the definition \"veteran\" any\nindividual who has received a DD Form 214.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date - 30th Day.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCounty veterans service agencies play and important role in our communi-\nties by helping those who have served in our nation's military and their\nfamily members access the resources available to them.  The intent of\nthis legislation is to allow a county supervisor to select a veteran who\nhas served in either peace time or war time as the director of county\nveteran services.\n\n \nCURRENT LAW\n\nUnder current law, county directors of veterans must have served during\nwartime.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Legislation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
